{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1367206-normal-knowledge-of-the-supernatural","id":1367206,"title":"Normal Knowledge of the Supernatural","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-02-12T06:38:31-08:00","id":1367206,"title":"Normal Knowledge of the Supernatural","content":"So, what does the normal person on the street know about the supernatural? Are we assuming that it's like the real world where most people are dubious of the idea of monsters, cryptids, etc running around? Or do people KNOW that the supernatural exists and SOMETHING is out there but just keep their heads down, lest they become one of its victims? Or somewhere in-between?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9255-docsteve2020","name":"DocSteve2020","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"25"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-12T07:48:14-08:00","id":1367223,"title":"","content":"I usally roll with whatever is floating around in pop culture. It &quot;exists&quot; but anyone who's a witness is usally viewed as some crack pot at best or someone out to make a quick buck at worst.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3953-dwight","name":"Dwight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3953_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2355"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-12T08:27:53-08:00","id":1367231,"title":"","content":"Most people try to rationalize it away if they saw something. An illusion, a trick of the light, drank too much, thinking they might be going crazy, a nightmare etc. They even subconsciously change their memory of the event. &quot;It was just a large dog. There are no Werewolves.&quot;, &quot;It was just a dream&quot;, etc.<br /> Especially NPCs need undeniable proof. Something experienced first hand, that they can not argue away.<br /> <br /> But since I don't like the idea of the players convincing NPCs to believe in the supernatural, I made it clear through my story, that normal people (most NPCs) can't handle that. (Supernatural encounters are a breaking point anyway.) When they first found a part of the God Machine, one NPC was accompanying them. The woman had a panic attack and a complete breakdown. The players had to get her into an ambulance. I am still considering that she will commit suicide or be a long-time patient in a mental hospital later.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Waiting for new Chronicles of Darkness Dice! \ud83e\udd17 \ud83c\udfb2","edited":{"userid":1825,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1825-elythia","user":"Elythia","date":". 02-12-2020, 11:31 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1825-elythia","name":"Elythia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1825_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"100"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-12T09:44:09-08:00","id":1367243,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DocSteve2020</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1367206-normal-knowledge-of-the-supernatural#post1367206\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Are we assuming that it's like the real world where most people are dubious of the idea of monsters, cryptids, etc running around?</div> </div> </div> </div>I think you're vastly overestimating how sceptical the general public is.<br /> <br /> The bigger issue is that an experience or belief doesn't really get you anywhere. The supernatural in CofD isn't a singular thing and is not terribly explicable without lots of in-setting information. A lot of the monsters have the names of traditional monsters but don't really conform to anything like what might be expected.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-12T10:05:17-08:00","id":1367249,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DocSteve2020</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1367206-normal-knowledge-of-the-supernatural#post1367206\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, what does the normal person on the street know about the supernatural? Are we assuming that it's like the real world where most people are dubious of the idea of monsters, cryptids, etc running around? Or do people KNOW that the supernatural exists and SOMETHING is out there but just keep their heads down, lest they become one of its victims? Or somewhere in-between?</div> </div> </div> </div>It's much closer to the second. Remember, the five questions asked to help clarify a normal person's Integrity standards is &quot;what brush with the supernatural have you experienced and repressed?&quot; The Chronicles of Darkness is a setting where almost everyone has at least one weird and spooky experience that is very hard to explain away, but which instills a deeper fear of the shadows. That doesn't mean they all <i>consciously</i> believe monsters are out there and they're just pretending they don't, and even those who consciously believe in the supernatural don't realize its full scope and reach. But the default state of a person in the Chronicles of Darkness is one of emotional denial.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}